Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

;
; Hardware Restriction Bypass Configuration
; 
; This registry file bypasses Windows 11 hardware requirements.
; Useful for installing Windows 11 on unsupported hardware like Intel 7700K.
;
; Usage:
; 1. For USB installation: Copy to USB root
; 2. For WIM injection: Import to registry of mounted image
; 3. Double-click to apply to current system before upgrade
;
; IMPORTANT: Bypassing requirements may result in:
; - Reduced security features
; - Potential compatibility issues
; - No official Microsoft support
;

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\Setup\LabConfig]
; Bypass TPM 2.0 requirement
"BypassTPMCheck"=dword:00000001

; Bypass Secure Boot requirement
"BypassSecureBootCheck"=dword:00000001

; Bypass RAM requirement (4GB minimum)
"BypassRAMCheck"=dword:00000001

; Bypass CPU generation requirement (Intel 8th Gen / AMD Zen 2)
"BypassCPUCheck"=dword:00000001

; Bypass storage requirement
"BypassStorageCheck"=dword:00000001

;
; Additional Windows 11 bypass (alternative location)
;
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\Setup\MoSetup]
"AllowUpgradesWithUnsupportedTPMOrCPU"=dword:00000001

;
; Note: These settings are specifically useful for:
; - Intel 7th Gen processors (Kaby Lake) like i7-7700K
; - Intel 6th Gen processors (Skylake)
; - Systems without TPM 2.0 module
; - Systems without Secure Boot support
; - Systems with less than 4GB RAM (not recommended)
;
